+- **The PGO trainer mirrors the server.** The profile is only as good as its match with the real
+  workload, so the trainer copies `app.rb` exactly: the same pragmas in the same order (`mmap_size`,
+  `cache_size` and `temp_store` included, so the mmap page path is trained at all), the same statement
+  text, and one `step` then `reset` per request instead of stepping to `DONE`. Its synthetic database
+  is seed-sized (50k users, 500k posts, 2M likes, with `ANALYZE`), post ids for reads and likes come
+  from the 20 newest posts as in the load test, and `__gcov_reset()` zeroes the counters after seeding
+  so the bulk-insert phase, which the server never runs, carries no weight. Measured at the SQLite
+  level this takes the feed statement from 18.9 to 17.9 µs; end to end it is about 0.4 µs per request
+  (under 1%), so it is paired-benchmarked rather than claimed. It adds about 10 s to `install.sh` and a
+  224 MB temporary database.
 - **One thread, and SQLite never releases the GVL.** Every query is an index lookup that takes
   microseconds, so releasing and reacquiring the GVL would cost more than it saves.
